TY  - RPRT
TI  - Soft-Prompt Personal Memory: Pluggable Factual Knowledge Injection via Prefix Tuning
AB  - We propose Soft-Prompt Personal Memory (SPPM), a lightweight method for injecting arbitrary factual knowledge into frozen large language models without modifying weights, retraining, or requiring external knowledge bases. Each fact is encoded as a compact set of 8 trainable virtual prefix tokens (80KB per memory entry), optimized end-to-end via prefix tuning with only 20,480 parameters trained per fact. The resulting memory cards are pluggable—loaded and unloaded at inference time by prepending their embeddings to the input, enabling dynamic multi-fact composition without interference. Experiments on Qwen3-4B-Instruct demonstrate perfect factual recall (100% hit rate) across multiple memory entries with zero cross-contamination, while requiring only 300 training steps per fact. We further show that the same prefix-tuning mechanism generalizes across entity types (persons, projects, technical concepts), establishing SPPM as a practical foundation for private, local, zero-latency personal knowledge injection.
