TI  - Effective Reinforcement Learning for Remote Sensing Vision-Language Models via Supervised Knowledge Injection
AB  - While Vision-Language Models (VLMs) have demonstrated impressive capabilities in general-domain visual understanding, their performance in remote sensing tasks remains limited due to domain discrepancies and the scarcity of remote sensing data in typical vision-language pretraining corpora. Recent advances show that reinforcement learning (RL) can enhance VLMs’ reasoning capabilities by guiding models to perform intermediate “thought” steps before answering. However, applying RL directly to remote sensing scenarios is often ineffective, as VLMs lack fundamental domain knowledge to begin with. To address this, we propose a novel paradigm that first equips VLMs with remote sensing knowledge in remote sensing visual grounding task through supervised fine-tuning (SFT) on a curated dataset of CoT samples specific to remote sensing. We then conduct RL to further strengthen the learned capabilities. Experiments on the in-domain dataset show that our RL-enhanced model outperforms its SFT-only counterpart. Furthermore, evaluations on the out-of-domain dataset demon-strate that our method fosters better generalization in remote sensing reasoning. Our approach offers a promising direction for adapting general-purpose VLMs to domain-specific visual understanding tasks.
