TI  - Graph Topology as Attention: Structured Knowledge Injection Beyond Text
AB  - Walk-encoded graph topology improves multi-hop reasoning by +0.468 over baseline while preserving sanity better than flat text (-0.133 vs. -0.333 degradation). A powered study (552 queries, 4 conditions, 3 runs) on Qwen3-30B establishes that knowledge graph structure is a viable injection channel for language models -- not by serializing the graph as text, but by encoding walks as cache tensors that the attention mechanism reads directly. A companion decomposition study on Qwen2.5-1.5B shows that direct KV-cache injection achieves perfect topology recovery (1.000), with K and V tensors contributing superadditively (each alone: 0.333; combined: 1.000). Scrambled controls confirm the signal is topological, not lexical -- the model is reading the graph, not the words.
